1
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:10,395
One changed requirement can change a machine's
behavior.

2
00:00:10,395 --> 00:00:16,590
But how do you prove the new software is
correct. This is Genesis RT: describe a
machine, generate native QNX software, and
prove it behaves.

3
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:24,270
Everything starts from a machine contract:
sensors, actuators, safety limits.

4
00:00:24,270 --> 00:00:28,340
The designer validates every field before
anything is built.

5
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,030
Genesis generates the QNX controller: guard
policy and build files.

6
00:00:38,030 --> 00:00:42,060
Each file carries its source hash, pinned
against the contract.

7
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:54,040
Then it runs for real: compiled with the QNX
toolchain, executed on QNX 8 under Q-Emu.

8
00:00:54,040 --> 00:00:59,280
Sixteen checks, a thousand performance
samples. Gate: PASS.

9
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:09,930
Now break it: a stale-sensor fault is injected
live. The guard answers; the run records it.

10
00:01:09,930 --> 00:01:14,360
A targeted verdict. Honest about what was not
re-tested.

11
00:01:17,300 --> 00:01:21,955
Diagnose with the evidence graph: every
verdict links back to scenarios, binaries,
requirements.

12
00:01:21,955 --> 00:01:26,610
Click any node: the proof behind the claim,
ready for review.

13
00:01:34,900 --> 00:01:40,985
Change one limit. 1. 2 to 1. 6 meters per
second.

14
00:01:40,985 --> 00:01:47,070
And verify both revisions. Before denies the
1. 5 command; after allows it. Same rigor, new
behavior. Two passports.

15
00:01:55,500 --> 00:02:00,960
A stale build bound to the new contract is
refused. No passport. Fail closed.

16
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:08,940
Both passports replay independently. No
servers, no trust-me step.

17
00:02:08,940 --> 00:02:15,580
Before and after verify clean: thirty-four
files, fifteen links each. Flip a single byte,
and the verifier rejects the pack. Evidence
you can defend.

18
00:02:24,300 --> 00:02:28,240
Specify. Compile. Run.

19
00:02:28,240 --> 00:02:32,180
Break. Prove. Genesis RT for QNX. Every
software change deserves a proof.
